                        "glosses": [
                            "A mass of cobwebs; anything that obscures the vision or is elaborate yet flimsy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7976975f-9008-4486-9d09-f45151191e1f",
                                "sense_id": "1ce76c51-32b5-35b7-9240-2d08ca4a5646",
                                "text": "When, across the hundredfold poor scepticisms, trivialisms and constitutional cobwebberies of Dryasdust, you catch any glimpse of a William the Conqueror, a Tancred of Hauteville or suchlike, — do you not discern veritably some rude outline of a true God-made King […]?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "28c7835c-70b7-4e27-b873-ec3c22e3f783",
                                "sense_id": "1ce76c51-32b5-35b7-9240-2d08ca4a5646",
                                "text": "Much of the cobwebbery of superstition, ancient and modern, is readily brushed away by this confident and sure hand; but there are other facts, facts of Christian consciousness, which do not, from our standpoint, disappear so readily."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
